# Converse Web Server

## Overview

The Web app (`Web,ff8`) is an optional HTTP server that gives users a browser
front-end to the BBS: browsing and downloading filebases, reading message areas,
and - when logged in - composing, replying to, and sending private messages, and
uploading files. It runs as a Wimp task alongside the Server and shares the Filer
databases and Support config.

Enable it with the `webserver yes` key in `<Converse$Dir>.Config.System`.

## Configuration / limits (compiled defaults)

| Setting | Default | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| Listen port          | 80 | `WEB_DEFAULT_PORT` |
| Document root        | `<Converse$Dir>.Web` | `WEB_DOCROOT` - stylesheet + template files |
| Max concurrent clients | 8 | `WEB_MAX_CLIENTS` |
| Max upload size      | 2 MB | `WEB_MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE` |
| Client timeout       | 60 s | `WEB_CLIENT_TIMEOUT` |

Activity is logged to `<Converse$Dir>.Logs.Web`.

## Page model

Most pages are generated in C from a shared "shell" (banner, Messages/Files nav,
breadcrumb, and a status line), so the whole site is one consistent look driven
by a single stylesheet served at `/style` (`style,f79`, filetype CSS &F79). The
navigation is a drill-down: Messages -> area -> message, mirrored for Files.

Only a couple of pages are still HTML template files under the document root
(`login,faf`, `upload,faf`); they contain `{{...}}` tags expanded per request
(see Template tags). Any other static file in the docroot is served directly.

## HTTP endpoints

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| GET  | `/` or `/messages`            | Message-area index (cards) |
| GET  | `/area/<base>/<area>`         | Message list for one area (newest first) |
| GET  | `/message/<base>/<area>/<id>` | Read a single message (Prev/Next, Reply) |
| GET  | `/compose/<base>/<area>`      | New-message form (login required) |
| GET  | `/reply/<base>/<area>/<id>`   | Reply form, pre-filled (login required) |
| POST | `/post`                       | Submit a new message / reply (login required) |
| GET  | `/files`                      | File-area listing |
| GET  | `/download/<base>/<id>/<name>`| Download a file |
| GET  | `/upload`                     | Upload form (login required) |
| POST | `/upload`                     | Upload a file into a filebase area (<= 2 MB) |
| GET  | `/api/areas?filebase=<n>`     | JSON list of accessible areas (used by the upload form) |
| GET  | `/login`                      | Login page |
| POST | `/login`                      | Authenticate; establishes a session |
| GET  | `/logout`                     | End the session |
| GET  | `/style`                      | Shared stylesheet (static) |

## Sessions

`/login` checks the supplied credentials against the user database (the same
accounts as the BBS). On success a cookie session (`CONVERSE_SESSION`) is created
and tracked server-side until `/logout` or timeout. The nav shows the logged-in
user with a logout link.

## Access control

Mirrors the BBS reader (`messagebase_can_read_message`):

- Public message areas are readable by anyone.
- Private-typed messages, and anything in a Private (areatype 4) or Netmail
  (areatype 2) area, are shown only to the sender or receiver, and require login.
- Restricted areas/messages honour the access level and keys of the logged-in
  user; unknown area types fail closed.
- Composing, replying and uploading require login. Posting to a public echo area
  stores the message unexported so the FTN scanner ships it to the network.
- Sending a private message resolves the recipient by username (`FIND_USERNAME`)
  and stores it typed PRIVATE addressed to that user.

## Template tags

The remaining template files (`login,faf`, `upload,faf`) may contain `{{...}}`
tags, expanded per request. A file is only processed if it contains `{{`.

| Tag | Expands to |
|-----|------------|
| `{{bbsname}}`     | The BBS name (from System config) |
| `{{loginform}}`   | Login/logout chip for the nav |
| `{{uploadform}}`  | The file-upload form HTML |

(The tag processor also still recognises `{{username}}`, `{{realname}}`,
`{{loggedin}}`, `{{loggedout}}`, `{{filebase}}`, `{{messagebase}}` and
`{{messageview}}` for backward compatibility, but the current drill-down and
message pages are generated in C rather than from template files.)

## Notes

- The server is intentionally small (single-threaded Wimp poll, capped client
  slots); it is a convenience front-end, not a general-purpose web server.
- File sizes are formatted with integer maths (this runtime has no floating-point
  `printf`); empty file/message areas are omitted from the listings.
